DESCRIPTION:[Podcast: This Week in Virology]\n\nIn his weekly clinical upd
 ate\, Daniel Griffin and Vincent Racaniello frustration continues over the
  increasing number of measles infections\, Kennedy’s undermining of vacc
 ines\, perpetuation of autism- vaccine\, autism-tylenol myths\, an outbrea
 k of hepatitis A virus in the US\, the Ebola outbreak in Uganda\, changes 
 in reporting of virus infection and vaccine recommendations\, Legionnaires
  disease and screw worm cases\, and before Dr. Griffin deep dives into rec
 ent statistics RSV\, influenza\, SARS-CoV-2 infections\, economics of a me
 asles outbreak in Chicago\, what defines reactogenicity of the mRNA COVID 
 vaccines\, the on-going delay by HHS of COVID shots for children\, neurops
 ychiatric symptoms of long COVID and contacting your federal government re
 presentative to stop the assault on science and biomedical research. Click
  arrow to play Download&nbsp\; TWiV 1360 (33 MB .mp3\, 54 min) Subscribe (
 free):&nbsp\; Apple Podcasts \, RSS \,&nbsp\; email Become a&nbsp\; patron
  &nbsp\;of&nbsp\;TWiV! Links for this episode CDC adds 177 cases to US mea
 sles total but has yet to confirm deaths in Pennsylvania (CIDRAP) Kennedy 
 questions vaccine safety at Children’s Health Defense event (CIDRAP) 2:3
 5 Trump says some routine immunizations will be split into five separate s
 hots. Vaccine experts say it won’t work (CNN) 5:41 Multistate Hepatitis 
 A Outbreak Potentially Linked to Frozen Clams (CDC: Hepatitis A) 10:17 Cum
 ulative Incidence and Prevalence of Autism Spectrum Disorder (JAMA Pediatr
 ics) 14:50 Data and Stat\n\nEvent URL: https://www.microbe.tv/twiv/twiv-13
 60/\n\nSource: twiv_podcast
