BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Children and Childhood in Colonial Senegal - Kelly Duke Bryant
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T210000
DTSTAMP:20261018T061310Z
UID:3fc2ea15387649ca@gid-seminars.wnprc.wisc.edu
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Presentation/Talk
DESCRIPTION:How did French colonial institutions seek to define\, regulate
 \, and ‘‘protect’’ childhood in Senegal\, and how did children res
 pond? \n\nIn this talk based on her recent book\, Negotiating Childhood: F
 rench Colonialism and African Children in Senegal\, 1848–1940\, Kelly Du
 ke Bryant explores the lived realities of African children across courts\,
  schools\, streets\, reformatories\, vaccine clinics\, and other sites of 
 colonial intervention. Rather than treating children as passive subjects\,
  Bryant illuminates the ways children limited or negotiated colonial refor
 ms and how the colonial state’s reliance on cooperation produced unexpec
 ted forms of resistance and accommodation. The talk highlights long-term c
 onsequences of colonial governance\, such as the privileging of chronologi
 cal age and the centrality of official documentation\, that continue to sh
 ape Senegalese childhoods.\n\nSpeaker Details\n\nKelly Duke Bryant is chai
 r of the History Department at Rowan University\, where she has taught sin
 ce 2009. She earned her MA in history from the University of Wisconsin and
  her Ph.D.\, also in history\, from Johns Hopkins University. A specialist
  in the history of West Africa\, she has published scholarly articles and 
 book chapters on the history of education\, childhood\, and youth in colon
 ial Senegal. She is the author of two books\, Education as Politics: Colon
 ial Schooling and Political Debate in Senegal\, 1850s-1914 (University of 
 Wisconsin Press\, 2015) and Negotiating Childhood: French Colonialism and 
 African Children in Senegal\, 1848-1940 (University of Massachusetts Press
 \, 2026). She recently began a term as president of the French Colonial Hi
 storical Society.\n\nEvent URL: https://events.stanford.edu/event/children
 -and-childhood-in-colonial-senegal-kelly-duke-bryant\n\nSource: stanford_v
 irtual
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/children-and-childhood-in-colonial-s
 enegal-kelly-duke-bryant
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Reminder: Children and Childhood in Colonial Senegal - Kelly D
 uke Bryant
TRIGGER:-PT1H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
